    "flow.逐个选择功能性生成资料": "Select references one by one",
    "flow.功能性生成允许按任务自由选资料。本教程指定“设定集”和“信息表”，请亲自勾选两个高亮文件。": "You can choose references to suit the task. For this tutorial, check the two highlighted files: setting notes “Worldbuilding.md” and facts “Facts.md”.",
    "flow.认识功能方向": "Explore task instructions",
    "flow.教程已提前写好示例要求。请点击输入框，了解这里用于说明要提炼的设定、边界和输出方向，不用再打字。": "Example instructions are already filled in. Click the input to see where to describe the setting details, boundaries and output direction to extract; no typing is needed.",
    "flow.生成功能内容": "Generate task content",
    "flow.请点击真实“生成内容”。教程播放预置设定。": "Click Generate content. The tutorial plays preset setting material.",
    "flow.查看大纲设定": "View outline settings",
    "flow.预置设定正在真实结果区流式展示。": "Preset setting material is appearing progressively in the result area.",
    "flow.保存功能内容": "Save task content",
    "flow.请点击真实保存按钮。教程只显示成功反馈。": "Click Save content. The tutorial only displays success feedback.",
    "flow.大纲设定与剧本": "Outline settings and scripts",
    "flow.大纲设定用于整理世界观、人物和写作边界；剧本用于生成分镜、场景和角色等剧本资料。": "Outline settings organize worldbuilding, characters and writing boundaries. Scripts generate storyboards, scenes, roles and other script material.",
    "flow.功能方向描述": "Task direction",
    "flow.这里用于明确拆解目标、写法要求或剧本要求，越具体越容易得到可用结果。": "Specify analysis goals, writing requirements or script requirements here. More specific instructions make usable results more likely.",
    "flow.功能也能参考作品资料": "Tasks can use work references too",
    "flow.功能性生成同样可以引用当前作品的设定、人物和信息资料。": "Story-element generation can also reference the current work’s setting, characters and facts.",
    "flow.复制、停止和重新生成": "Copy, stop and regenerate",
    "flow.生成过程中主按钮会变成停止；完成后可以复制结果，再次点击生成可获取另一版。": "During generation the main button becomes Stop. After completion, copy the result or click Generate again for another version.",
    "flow.您完成了功能类型、题材、真实模板、关联文件、方向描述、模型、模拟生成和教程内保存。": "You practiced selecting a function, genre, real template, linked files, task direction and model, then simulated generation and saving within the tutorial.",
